1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
To be continued...

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,480
Enough! I can't even hear myself think!

3
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:36,960
If you're not here to work, then go home!

4
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:41,780
What do you think, Julie?

5
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:43,920
Who the hell do you think you're talking to, Mia?

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:48,300
Sorry, you're right. We'll try to keep the noise down as long as we're all in the classroom.

7
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:49,740
Hey, Srono.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:29,980
What do you think you're talking to?

9
00:02:58,030 --> 00:03:16,150
Hey, give it a rest. No need to pick on that poor turtle.

10
00:03:16,690 --> 00:03:18,490
Huh? Hell are you supposed to be?

11
00:03:19,950 --> 00:03:22,490
Oh, wait. I think that might be Quackmire.

12
00:03:22,810 --> 00:03:26,410
It doesn't matter who started it. Only cowards gang up like that.

13
00:03:28,030 --> 00:03:30,330
Huh. Let's go.

14
00:03:37,330 --> 00:03:38,570
Are you all right?

15
00:03:44,190 --> 00:03:46,570
At what point did it sound like I wanted your...

16
00:03:48,570 --> 00:03:52,790
Sorry. I'm fine. Thank you.

17
00:03:53,330 --> 00:03:54,890
Yeah, no problem at all.

18
00:03:54,890 --> 00:03:58,030
I figured he was going to snap at me.

19
00:03:58,770 --> 00:04:00,750
Has he finally realized I'm not his enemy?

20
00:04:01,190 --> 00:04:03,610
What'd I do to upset him so much in the first place?

21
00:04:06,270 --> 00:04:07,450
Well, whatever.

22
00:04:07,450 --> 00:04:29,350
Hey.

23
00:04:29,350 --> 00:04:42,850
So, um, there's this girl I like.

24
00:04:43,350 --> 00:04:43,830
Okay.

25
00:04:44,370 --> 00:04:46,510
Is it me? It's not me, right?

26
00:04:47,170 --> 00:04:49,610
Maybe he just wants help writing a love letter or something.

27
00:04:50,230 --> 00:04:50,490
Yeah.

28
00:04:50,490 --> 00:04:54,710
That's her there.

29
00:04:55,870 --> 00:04:56,910
Oh, good for...

30
00:04:56,910 --> 00:05:03,650
You poor guy.

31
00:05:04,330 --> 00:05:05,470
That is my love.

32
00:05:05,590 --> 00:05:07,050
Lady Alina Lee's Dragon Road.

33
00:05:07,210 --> 00:05:09,990
A name nearly as beautiful and bold as the woman who bears it.

34
00:05:10,230 --> 00:05:11,950
She's studious as her grades can attest.

35
00:05:12,170 --> 00:05:15,410
And as an adventurer, she grasps the practicalities of magical combat.

36
00:05:15,410 --> 00:05:16,730
How I admire her!

37
00:05:17,090 --> 00:05:17,530
Uh-huh.

38
00:05:18,170 --> 00:05:20,410
I hoped I was mistaken, but nope.

39
00:05:20,470 --> 00:05:22,250
He really does mean Alina Lee's.

40
00:05:23,050 --> 00:05:23,370
Oof.

41
00:05:25,210 --> 00:05:29,790
There have been some scurrilous rumors about her taking any male student who looks at her twice as a lover.

42
00:05:30,270 --> 00:05:32,070
And some of the professors as well.

43
00:05:32,450 --> 00:05:34,410
I've tried to intervene, but...

44
00:05:35,410 --> 00:05:37,510
Sorry, bud, but those were no rumors.

45
00:05:37,510 --> 00:05:40,270
So, what do you want me to do?

46
00:05:41,270 --> 00:05:43,570
Oh, well, you know her, right?

47
00:05:44,150 --> 00:05:45,970
So, would you...

48
00:05:45,970 --> 00:05:47,350
Mind introducing us?

49
00:05:51,850 --> 00:05:53,150
Romantic advice?

50
00:05:53,990 --> 00:05:55,450
Uh, why?

51
00:05:55,650 --> 00:05:56,950
Do you have a crush on someone?

52
00:05:57,950 --> 00:06:00,390
No, but a classmate of mine does.

53
00:06:00,730 --> 00:06:01,350
Who's that?

54
00:06:02,030 --> 00:06:06,570
As long as this stays between us, it's Cliff, one of the other special students.

55
00:06:06,570 --> 00:06:08,530
Oh, yes, I know him.

56
00:06:09,150 --> 00:06:10,070
Please, continue.

57
00:06:10,530 --> 00:06:14,470
The way he tells it, he fell in love with this woman immediately, at first sight.

58
00:06:14,790 --> 00:06:18,730
And I'm kind of close with the person he fell for, but I'm not sure about introducing them.

59
00:06:19,190 --> 00:06:21,930
I just don't want him to think it's because I want her to myself.

60
00:06:22,410 --> 00:06:24,770
Do you have any idea how I should navigate this?

61
00:06:25,130 --> 00:06:29,410
Well, I suppose I should ask, where does your hesitation come from?

62
00:06:29,630 --> 00:06:33,730
I have nothing against her, but she has some issues that make her a tricky match.

63
00:06:33,730 --> 00:06:34,410
I see.

64
00:06:35,150 --> 00:06:40,450
You know, even if a trait is unappealing to you, that doesn't necessarily mean it would be to Cliff.

65
00:06:42,010 --> 00:06:46,730
From what I hear, most people couldn't imagine dating the person I like, but...

66
00:06:47,390 --> 00:06:48,910
Master Fitz has a crush?

67
00:06:49,210 --> 00:06:50,510
I wonder who it is.

68
00:06:50,910 --> 00:06:53,070
Princess Ariel is probably the safest bet.

69
00:06:53,070 --> 00:06:57,370
And it's hard to see someone around all the time and feel like they're out of reach.

70
00:06:57,690 --> 00:07:01,530
So yeah, I'd say, go ahead and introduce them in that way.

71
00:07:01,630 --> 00:07:04,250
He would at least have an opportunity to express himself.

72
00:07:04,830 --> 00:07:05,370
You think?

73
00:07:05,650 --> 00:07:08,190
I'm afraid that could lead to all sorts of trouble down the road.

74
00:07:08,350 --> 00:07:09,630
That's not your burden, though.

75
00:07:09,910 --> 00:07:14,230
I mean, once you get them in a room together, they have to figure out the next steps for themselves.

76
00:07:14,630 --> 00:07:16,470
Yeah, he does kind of have a point there.

77
00:07:16,470 --> 00:07:17,990
I guess you're right.

78
00:07:18,330 --> 00:07:19,310
Thank you, Master Fitz.

79
00:07:19,390 --> 00:07:20,450
I appreciate the input.

80
00:07:20,710 --> 00:07:21,390
Oh, please.

81
00:07:21,870 --> 00:07:23,890
I'm just glad I was able to help at all.

82
00:07:24,190 --> 00:07:24,470
So...

83
00:07:24,470 --> 00:07:43,930
Hey there, Rudeus.

84
00:07:43,930 --> 00:07:45,770
What a lovely surprise.

85
00:07:46,250 --> 00:07:47,610
You don't often call on me.

86
00:07:47,950 --> 00:07:48,870
And who is this?

87
00:07:49,550 --> 00:07:50,730
All right, good luck in there.

88
00:07:51,010 --> 00:07:52,330
Just remember I did warn you.

89
00:07:52,330 --> 00:07:55,730
So if this goes poorly in any way, please don't take that out on me.

90
00:07:55,910 --> 00:07:56,590
Of course.

91
00:07:56,790 --> 00:07:58,310
I'm fully prepared for rejection.

92
00:07:59,950 --> 00:08:01,050
Hello, Alina-Lise.

93
00:08:01,350 --> 00:08:03,190
I would like you to meet Cliff Grimoire.

94
00:08:03,450 --> 00:08:05,650
He's one of the special students and a year ahead of me.

95
00:08:05,950 --> 00:08:07,170
It's an honor, my lady.

96
00:08:07,510 --> 00:08:08,830
As he said, I am Cliff.

97
00:08:09,130 --> 00:08:10,110
Oh, my.

98
00:08:10,330 --> 00:08:12,210
What a perfect gentleman you are.

99
00:08:12,770 --> 00:08:14,650
My name's Alina-Lise Dragonroad.

100
00:08:15,390 --> 00:08:19,410
Now then, what brings you to see me this fine afternoon, Master Cliff?

101
00:08:19,410 --> 00:08:24,290
He's been interested in meeting you for some time, so I thought I'd introduce you.

102
00:08:24,410 --> 00:08:24,770
Indeed.

103
00:08:25,090 --> 00:08:28,450
I've spent many an evening admiring your radiant beauty from across the courtyard.

104
00:08:28,810 --> 00:08:31,250
I beg you to consider a personal relationship with me.

105
00:08:35,590 --> 00:08:36,030
Huh?

106
00:08:38,410 --> 00:08:38,850
Really?

107
00:08:39,050 --> 00:08:39,710
Really what?

108
00:08:39,790 --> 00:08:41,170
How much do you want for him?

109
00:08:41,410 --> 00:08:43,750
She thinks I'm here to pimp my upperclassmen?

110
00:08:43,930 --> 00:08:44,730
Now that's low.

111
00:08:44,990 --> 00:08:46,130
That's not what this is.

112
00:08:46,270 --> 00:08:47,590
You can't mean that.

113
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:49,410
Rudeus, you know what I'm like.

114
00:08:49,470 --> 00:08:51,190
I really can't commit to anyone.

115
00:08:51,830 --> 00:08:54,730
Why would you bring this naive little choir boy here?

116
00:08:54,890 --> 00:08:55,830
That's just cruel.

117
00:08:56,230 --> 00:08:57,890
Now I'm the shameless one?

118
00:08:58,050 --> 00:08:59,250
I'm not trying to trick him.

119
00:08:59,430 --> 00:09:01,890
I am just introducing him like he asked me to.

120
00:09:02,110 --> 00:09:02,830
You mean it?

121
00:09:03,530 --> 00:09:06,310
Yeah, I'll even swear by Master Roxy if you like.

122
00:09:07,430 --> 00:09:09,950
Well, if he's serious, that's also a problem.

123
00:09:10,490 --> 00:09:12,250
People shouldn't have feelings for me.

124
00:09:12,630 --> 00:09:13,610
That's a surprise.

125
00:09:13,830 --> 00:09:17,990
I figured she'd say that she had an in-or-something book just in case and whisk him away.

126
00:09:18,330 --> 00:09:20,630
You didn't forget about my curse, did you?

127
00:09:20,770 --> 00:09:23,430
It's not compatible with an exclusive relationship.

128
00:09:24,750 --> 00:09:26,510
Yeah, that's too bad, isn't it?

129
00:09:26,670 --> 00:09:28,250
Guess you'll just have to turn him down.

130
00:09:28,530 --> 00:09:29,370
You wouldn't mind?

131
00:09:29,630 --> 00:09:31,970
That won't cause any bad blood between you two?

132
00:09:32,310 --> 00:09:33,590
Nope, it's not a problem.

133
00:09:34,070 --> 00:09:36,770
But I do think you should tell him exactly why.

134
00:09:38,170 --> 00:09:39,190
I can do that.

135
00:09:39,190 --> 00:09:46,830
Rudeus, please see yourself out so that Cliff and I may speak in private.

136
00:09:47,310 --> 00:09:47,450
Huh?

137
00:09:47,670 --> 00:09:48,690
Oh, yeah, of course.

138
00:09:49,370 --> 00:09:51,310
Excuse me, I'll be just outside.

139
00:09:53,830 --> 00:09:54,790
And Rudeus?

140
00:09:55,330 --> 00:09:56,750
Thank you, I mean that.

141
00:09:58,010 --> 00:10:00,870
The gratitude in his voice makes my chest ache.

142
00:10:00,870 --> 00:10:14,130
Hey, Zanobar, are you here?

143
00:10:14,130 --> 00:10:21,550
Ha, good morning, Rudeus.

144
00:10:22,310 --> 00:10:26,090
As you can clearly see, we've chosen to become a couple.

145
00:10:26,430 --> 00:10:27,510
Okay, why?

146
00:10:27,750 --> 00:10:33,430
There was such a fire and passion to his proposal that it pierced and melted even my most frozen heart of hearts.

147
00:10:34,410 --> 00:10:35,990
Congratulations, I'm happy for you.

148
00:10:36,070 --> 00:10:37,470
But what about your curse?

149
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:40,250
A curse is nothing in the face of true love.

150
00:10:40,630 --> 00:10:43,090
For Cliff's sake, I'll do my best to control myself.

151
00:10:43,830 --> 00:10:46,410
If your heart belongs to me, nothing else matters.

152
00:10:46,790 --> 00:10:49,230
And I swear to you, I will lift your curse one day.

153
00:10:50,090 --> 00:10:50,910
Oh, Cliff.

154
00:10:51,930 --> 00:10:52,930
Oh, Adlina Lise.

155
00:10:52,930 --> 00:11:03,830
If this works for them, then who am I to interfere?

156
00:11:07,970 --> 00:11:12,630
And if I'm being honest, I would also love to break my curse and get busy with someone.

157
00:11:22,930 --> 00:11:27,290
Wow, they're so intense.

158
00:11:27,290 --> 00:11:33,090
All is upon us, and Beast Folk mating rituals are in full swing.

159
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:39,090
Namely, a one-on-one duel that acts as a marriage proposal and determines who will lead the resulting family.

160
00:11:39,510 --> 00:11:40,530
In other words, they're in heat.

161
00:11:41,030 --> 00:11:43,750
Which brings me to my two absent classmates.

162
00:11:45,110 --> 00:11:48,030
Lenia and Persina are princesses of the Doldia tribe.

163
00:11:48,030 --> 00:11:54,970
The Beast Folk all adore them, and despite their public disinterest in marriage, they're inundated with challenges from suitors every year.

164
00:11:55,670 --> 00:11:59,770
So they wrote to let me know that they wouldn't be leaving the girls' dorm for a while.

165
00:12:00,270 --> 00:12:02,890
But they also said, the rest is up to you.

166
00:12:03,450 --> 00:12:05,010
And I don't know what that means.

167
00:12:12,090 --> 00:12:14,830
I take it that you, sir, are Quagmire Rudeus.

168
00:12:15,210 --> 00:12:17,490
I challenge you to a matrimonial duel.

169
00:12:18,030 --> 00:12:28,670
Is this one of those proposal challenges that have been kind of in vogue around campus lately, or...?

170
00:12:28,670 --> 00:12:29,270
Indeed.

171
00:12:30,850 --> 00:12:35,970
I beg your pardon, but I'm actually straight, you see, so I'm gonna be going...

172
00:12:35,970 --> 00:12:37,950
You have no right to refuse!

173
00:12:38,350 --> 00:12:42,110
I wrote to Lady Persina, and she informed me that you're the boss of her pack.

174
00:12:42,410 --> 00:12:44,910
Thus, you are duty-bound to accept all challengers.

175
00:12:44,910 --> 00:12:47,290
Oh, that's what they meant.

176
00:12:47,670 --> 00:12:48,150
Jerks.

177
00:12:49,150 --> 00:12:50,650
Now draw your weapon!

178
00:12:51,550 --> 00:12:56,550
Well, better luck next year, I suppose.

179
00:12:56,550 --> 00:13:05,050
Hey, Rudeus.

180
00:13:05,410 --> 00:13:06,930
Have you seen this line outside?

181
00:13:07,470 --> 00:13:08,330
What did you do?

182
00:13:08,330 --> 00:13:14,230
I didn't do anything, but apparently whoever beats me gets to marry Linia and or Persina.

183
00:13:14,570 --> 00:13:15,350
No, really?

184
00:13:15,810 --> 00:13:18,230
There's no way you have the authority to allow that.

185
00:13:18,470 --> 00:13:20,850
That's for the chief of the Doldia tribe to decide.

186
00:13:21,350 --> 00:13:25,010
Well, they've been redirecting all their personal challenges to me either way.

187
00:13:26,150 --> 00:13:29,850
Gauntlet of highly motivated horny alpha males, here I come!

188
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:32,950
Oh, well, it isn't all men, from what I could see.

189
00:13:33,150 --> 00:13:35,150
There was at least one girl out there.

190
00:13:35,530 --> 00:13:36,170
Wait, really?

191
00:13:36,630 --> 00:13:37,250
Is she cute?

192
00:13:38,270 --> 00:13:38,630
Wow.

193
00:13:39,670 --> 00:13:41,810
You really are your father's son.

194
00:13:43,410 --> 00:13:44,750
Hey, sorry, what'd you say?

195
00:13:49,530 --> 00:13:50,830
Hey, Master Fitz!

196
00:13:51,270 --> 00:13:51,710
Ugh!

197
00:13:53,170 --> 00:13:55,070
What the heck?

198
00:13:55,070 --> 00:14:02,870
Your courage is a credit to you.

199
00:14:03,250 --> 00:14:07,150
This university of magic attracts some truly stout-hearted fellows.

200
00:14:08,370 --> 00:14:09,370
What, uh...

201
00:14:10,510 --> 00:14:10,790
Hmm?

202
00:14:11,470 --> 00:14:12,090
Heh heh.

203
00:14:12,450 --> 00:14:12,750
Hello!

204
00:14:13,310 --> 00:14:17,430
They said I had to defeat them all if I didn't want to wait my turn to see you.

205
00:14:17,610 --> 00:14:19,930
And here you are, right on cue.

206
00:14:20,390 --> 00:14:21,910
Yes, the Eye of Foresight.

207
00:14:22,130 --> 00:14:23,610
You must be Rudeus Greyrat.

208
00:14:23,610 --> 00:14:28,870
My fiancée, Kishirika Kishirisu, great emperor of the demon world, speaks well of you.

209
00:14:29,330 --> 00:14:31,590
I am the demon king, Barigari.

210
00:14:32,150 --> 00:14:34,410
And I've come to challenge you to a duel.

211
00:14:35,630 --> 00:14:36,610
What is happening?

212
00:14:41,610 --> 00:14:42,050
Hmm.

213
00:14:42,390 --> 00:14:43,310
Must we wait?

214
00:14:43,890 --> 00:14:44,610
Forgive me.

215
00:14:44,990 --> 00:14:47,610
Someone is on their way to fetch my staff for me right now.

216
00:14:47,610 --> 00:14:49,870
You humans can be so hasty.

217
00:14:49,990 --> 00:14:51,590
I expected to be shooed away.

218
00:14:51,910 --> 00:14:53,650
But you seem quite composed.

219
00:14:53,970 --> 00:14:56,470
No wonder my fiancée thinks so highly of you.

220
00:14:56,730 --> 00:14:57,610
And you said...

221
00:14:58,170 --> 00:15:00,910
Your fiancée is Empress Kishirika, didn't you?

222
00:15:01,210 --> 00:15:01,730
Yes.

223
00:15:02,070 --> 00:15:05,490
Her majesty bestowed this demon eye on me, though we only met briefly.

224
00:15:05,490 --> 00:15:09,910
She described you as something of a magical marvel.

225
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:13,830
She hasn't spoken of anyone with such excitement in a long while.

226
00:15:14,610 --> 00:15:15,790
I'm no one special.

227
00:15:16,370 --> 00:15:19,630
I may have a bit more mana than the average person, but...

228
00:15:19,630 --> 00:15:27,850
Please be seated.

229
00:15:29,430 --> 00:15:31,010
More marvelous than Laplace.

230
00:15:31,610 --> 00:15:34,950
That's how she first described you to me, without a moment's hesitation.

231
00:15:35,690 --> 00:15:37,650
She's never said that of anyone else before,

232
00:15:37,830 --> 00:15:41,330
which means your mana capacity must be among the greatest in the world.

233
00:15:41,550 --> 00:15:42,630
Wow, is that so?

234
00:15:43,270 --> 00:15:47,050
Granted, I have been training non-stop to improve it for most of my life now.

235
00:15:47,050 --> 00:15:50,770
No amount of training would allow you or anyone else to rival Laplace.

236
00:15:51,310 --> 00:15:53,070
For most, it's simply impossible.

237
00:15:53,890 --> 00:15:54,130
Okay.

238
00:15:55,150 --> 00:15:58,890
Even if most people can't do it, what about reincarnated people like me?

239
00:15:59,290 --> 00:16:01,990
Maybe the man-god hooked me up with some sweet hacks or something.

240
00:16:02,510 --> 00:16:05,930
Come to think of it, your majesty, may I ask you about a certain name?

241
00:16:06,550 --> 00:16:11,770
And, um, to be clear, I'm not an agent or a minion or anything of this person I'm thinking about,

242
00:16:11,910 --> 00:16:15,750
so please don't attack me for simply mentioning them, if you wouldn't mind?

243
00:16:15,750 --> 00:16:18,230
I said begin our duel until you're armed.

244
00:16:18,710 --> 00:16:20,290
You have the Demon King's word.

245
00:16:21,410 --> 00:16:25,530
Does the name man-god mean anything at all to you?

246
00:16:27,390 --> 00:16:28,310
Man-god?

247
00:16:28,770 --> 00:16:30,990
How is it that you came to learn this name, boy?

248
00:16:31,670 --> 00:16:33,230
They appear in my dreams.

249
00:16:33,910 --> 00:16:35,790
Hmm, in your dreams, huh?

250
00:16:35,990 --> 00:16:36,550
I see.

251
00:16:36,990 --> 00:16:38,450
What do you know about them?

252
00:16:38,850 --> 00:16:41,830
Hmm, nothing.

253
00:16:43,050 --> 00:16:44,190
Ah, that's too bad.

254
00:16:44,190 --> 00:16:45,130
Indeed.

255
00:16:47,730 --> 00:16:49,690
What a sad fellow you are.

256
00:16:49,990 --> 00:16:51,230
Clamming up all of a sudden.

257
00:16:51,690 --> 00:16:52,790
Laugh with me, boy!

258
00:16:52,790 --> 00:17:10,890
Here's your staff. I'm sorry it took so long to find it.

259
00:17:11,010 --> 00:17:14,350
No, that's quite all right. I appreciate you running to get it.

260
00:17:16,390 --> 00:17:21,030
Please don't do anything rash. If it looks like you'll lose, just grovel and beg for mercy.

261
00:17:21,030 --> 00:17:23,410
No one will think less of you for it, I promise.

262
00:17:24,490 --> 00:17:25,330
Your Majesty?

263
00:17:26,270 --> 00:17:27,730
Call me Body Boy.

264
00:17:28,390 --> 00:17:31,390
Uh, sir, Body, then. I have a request.

265
00:17:31,810 --> 00:17:32,770
Speak your piece.

266
00:17:33,250 --> 00:17:36,850
Even if I lose to you, I would ask that you please spare my life.

267
00:17:39,170 --> 00:17:43,030
Begging for mercy before we begin. You're a funny one, aren't you?

268
00:17:43,690 --> 00:17:45,550
Life is a tragic thing to waste.

269
00:17:45,910 --> 00:17:51,310
You're so sure you'll lose. One would think such a large monopool would lend a man some confidence.

270
00:17:52,130 --> 00:17:56,450
About two years ago, I fought a man known as the Dragon God and barely made it out alive.

271
00:17:59,090 --> 00:18:02,710
Crap. He didn't react to the name Man God, but does he know Orsted?

272
00:18:03,210 --> 00:18:05,130
I think I might have hit a nerve.

273
00:18:06,510 --> 00:18:09,830
All right. I have a proposal for the terms of our duel.

274
00:18:09,830 --> 00:18:11,990
What might that be?

275
00:18:12,950 --> 00:18:14,310
Just one blow.

276
00:18:15,130 --> 00:18:15,490
Huh?

277
00:18:16,490 --> 00:18:20,310
Strike me once. Attack me with the force of your mightiest blow.

278
00:18:20,970 --> 00:18:23,790
Perhaps use a spell you used against the Dragon God.

279
00:18:24,370 --> 00:18:27,290
If you can manage to wound me, then you will be named the Victor.

280
00:18:28,810 --> 00:18:31,890
That sounds reasonable. I accept your conditions.

281
00:18:34,190 --> 00:18:34,710
Good.

282
00:18:34,710 --> 00:18:34,770
Good.

283
00:18:39,830 --> 00:18:44,590
Against Orsted, I was unarmed, one-handed, and panicking.

284
00:18:45,210 --> 00:18:48,750
But here, I can channel everything I have into this shot.

285
00:18:49,490 --> 00:18:52,510
Creating the bullet is fundamentally no different than crafting a figure.

286
00:18:53,150 --> 00:18:56,510
I'll focus on hardness and aerodynamics, then rotate it.

287
00:18:57,070 --> 00:19:00,890
The faster I can make it spin, the better penetration it will have on contact.

288
00:19:01,550 --> 00:19:03,610
But velocity is the most critical aspect.

289
00:19:04,030 --> 00:19:06,630
I've never used this much mana for speed before.

290
00:19:06,630 --> 00:19:16,350
All right. Get ready.

291
00:19:17,130 --> 00:19:18,770
Excellent. Go on.

292
00:19:33,770 --> 00:19:34,850
No way.

293
00:19:36,630 --> 00:19:38,030
Is he dead?

294
00:19:51,070 --> 00:19:52,930
Buddy Daddy has revived!

295
00:19:53,350 --> 00:19:54,350
Oh, you're alive.

296
00:19:55,350 --> 00:19:57,530
Yes, I thought I was a goner!

297
00:19:57,530 --> 00:20:06,930
You've vanquished me in single combat, Brutus.

298
00:20:07,190 --> 00:20:08,990
So you may call yourself a hero.

299
00:20:09,250 --> 00:20:11,130
I don't think I will, but thanks.

300
00:20:11,130 --> 00:20:13,490
Then at least let out a victory cheer for the crowd.

301
00:20:13,490 --> 00:20:14,850
Ha ha ha ha ha!

302
00:20:16,850 --> 00:20:17,390
Okay.

303
00:20:17,930 --> 00:20:20,650
If he says I won, I guess I won.

304
00:20:20,990 --> 00:20:22,510
Um, I'm the winner!

305
00:20:22,510 --> 00:20:24,870
Well done!

306
00:20:25,090 --> 00:20:26,850
Now it's my turn to take a whack.

307
00:20:28,670 --> 00:20:28,990
Huh?

308
00:20:30,490 --> 00:20:30,970
Ha ha!

309
00:20:30,970 --> 00:20:31,190
Ha ha ha!

310
00:20:36,470 --> 00:20:36,950
There.

311
00:20:37,470 --> 00:20:38,710
Is the pain gone, too?

312
00:20:39,030 --> 00:20:39,830
Yeah, it is.

313
00:20:39,930 --> 00:20:40,330
Thank you.

314
00:20:41,690 --> 00:20:46,790
Well, healing aside, after the day you just had, I would advise taking it easy tonight.

315
00:20:46,790 --> 00:20:49,770
I really can't thank you enough for all your help, Master Fitz.

316
00:20:57,850 --> 00:20:59,090
He's probably right.

317
00:20:59,430 --> 00:21:02,610
Between duels and Demon Kings, I've had one hell of a day.

318
00:21:02,610 --> 00:21:06,610
But hey, at least I'll probably never see Body Gotti again.

319
00:21:17,670 --> 00:21:19,330
I'm you, you could do it, boss!

320
00:21:19,670 --> 00:21:22,590
A whole mating season, and we didn't even have to lift a finger!

321
00:21:22,870 --> 00:21:26,770
But I never expected a Demon King would show up to challenge you for our hand.

322
00:21:26,850 --> 00:21:29,810
I suppose our charms really must reach all corners of the world.

323
00:21:29,810 --> 00:21:32,670
Well, as thanks, I invite you to touch Lenea's boobs.

324
00:21:32,870 --> 00:21:33,350
Thank you.

325
00:21:33,430 --> 00:21:34,210
That's very generous.

326
00:21:34,890 --> 00:21:35,350
Yee-haw!

327
00:21:41,750 --> 00:21:42,310
Huh?

328
00:21:42,390 --> 00:21:44,950
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

329
00:21:46,050 --> 00:21:47,330
Ha ha ha ha ha ha!

330
00:21:47,330 --> 00:21:48,170
Ha ha ha ha ha ha!

331
00:21:48,870 --> 00:21:49,670
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

332
00:21:49,670 --> 00:21:50,430
Ha ha ha ha ha ha!

333
00:21:50,430 --> 00:21:52,330
The immortal Demon King Body Gotti has returned!

334
00:21:54,470 --> 00:21:55,990
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

335
00:21:55,990 --> 00:21:58,090
Ha ha ha ha ha ha!

336
00:21:58,090 --> 00:22:02,090
Goddamn it.

337
00:23:36,020 --> 00:23:40,020
La-ya-la-ya-la

